<x-public-layout title="Privacy Policy">
<article class="reference-container ats-guide policy-document">
<header class="ats-guide-intro"><span class="reference-eyebrow">HOW YOUR INFORMATION IS HANDLED</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="policy-status">Effective date: 16 October 2026</p><p><strong>Code Dev Solutions</strong> operates <strong>atscvdetector.com</strong> and determines why and how personal information is processed for this service. This policy covers our accounts, CV builder, matching tools, optional rewriting and support. Email <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a> with “Privacy request” in the subject for questions or requests.</p></header>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>1. Information we process</h2><ul class="ats-guide-checklist"><li><strong>Account details:</strong> name, email address, hashed password where used, verification details and account records.</li><li><strong>Google sign-in:</strong> if selected, your Google identifier, name, email address and verification status. This flow does not request Gmail messages, contacts or Drive files. We do not receive your Google password.</li><li><strong>Career information:</strong> documents, extracted text, contact details, employment and education history, skills, references, job descriptions, edits and generated drafts you supply or request.</li><li><strong>Saved work and sessions:</strong> builder drafts, saved CV versions and information needed to continue a workflow. Sign in and verify your account to use the builder.</li><li><strong>Technical records:</strong> IP addresses, browser or device information, session identifiers, request times and diagnostic or security records where generated by the application or hosting systems.</li><li><strong>Support messages:</strong> your email, message and any attachments you send. Paid checkout is disabled; future payments require updated information about the provider and transaction records.</li></ul></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>2. Why we use information</h2><p>We use it to create and secure accounts, verify emails, recover access, build and export CVs, compare text with job descriptions, provide requested rewriting, save your work and answer enquiries. Necessary processing also prevents abuse, diagnoses faults and meets applicable obligations.</p><p>Depending on the activity and applicable law, processing grounds include providing a requested service or performing a contract, consent where required, compliance with legal obligations and legitimate operational or security interests where permitted and balanced against your rights. Agreeing to terms is not consent to every possible use of your data.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>3. Optional external AI processing</h2><p>Match scores are calculated within our application. When you request AI analysis or rewriting, relevant CV text, the job description, confirmed skills and analysis details are sent to OpenAI (or the configured rewriting provider). Returned content may be held in your session and saved when you choose to continue into the builder.</p><p>External processing may take place outside Zimbabwe. A provider's applicable terms govern its own handling, security and retention. Before personal information is submitted, the AI feature's notice must identify the applicable provider and data-use terms. External providers may retain content or use it to improve services, depending on the applicable service terms. Ask support if those details are unclear, and avoid the AI feature until you understand the disclosed processing.</p><p>Remove unnecessary sensitive data, identity numbers, financial details and third-party contacts. Using the non-AI builder or basic comparison is separate from choosing AI rewriting. Withdrawing consent stops future consent-based processing but cannot reverse a completed request.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>4. Who may receive information</h2><p>Hosting and infrastructure suppliers, email delivery providers, your selected sign-in provider, AI providers for requested functions and authorised support personnel may process information needed for their roles, under appropriate arrangements. Public pages also load Google-hosted fonts; your browser sends connection information such as your IP address to Google for that request.</p><p>We do not sell CVs, provide a public CV directory or send your CV to employers as part of these tools. Information may be disclosed when lawfully required, to address security incidents or protect legal rights, or during a business transfer with appropriate safeguards and required notice. Advertising or unrelated marketing use would need a separate lawful basis and clear notice.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>5. Cookies and sessions</h2><p>Essential cookies and server-side sessions maintain sign-in, protect forms and connect editing steps. Blocking or deleting them can sign you out, interrupt a workflow or make an unsaved draft unavailable. A sign-in provider can separately use cookies on its own service.</p><p>The current application does not include advertising trackers or third-party behavioural analytics. If optional tracking is introduced, we will explain it and seek consent where required before enabling it.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>6. Storage and retention</h2><p>This is an account-based service. Saved CV content is stored so you can reopen and edit it. Uploaded files, extracted text, drafts and generated documents may also exist in temporary storage or sessions during processing. Closing a browser tab does not guarantee erasure. We do not describe all processing as storage-free or immediately deleted.</p><p>We retain account information and saved content while needed to provide your account, unless you request deletion or another lawful retention reason applies. Sessions, temporary files, logs and support records serve different purposes and may remain for different periods.</p><p>On a verified deletion request, we remove or anonymise information no longer needed, subject to lawful exceptions. Disputes, security incidents, statutory obligations and restricted backups may justify limited retention for those purposes. Contact support for information about retention periods and backup handling relevant to your request.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>7. Security and international processing</h2><p>The application uses password hashing, authenticated access, document ownership checks and request protections. No website or transmission method guarantees absolute security. Protect your device and email account, and never disclose credentials to support.</p><p>Providers may process data in countries with different privacy laws. We must assess the deployment against applicable Zimbabwean cross-border requirements and any required safeguards. We will provide personal data breach notifications where law requires them. This policy is not a claim of regulatory certification or a guarantee against incidents.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>8. Your choices and rights</h2><p>Depending on applicable law and exceptions, you may request access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection to certain processing, withdrawal of consent and portability where provided by law. You can update details in your profile. Password accounts can request deletion there; if Google sign-in prevents password confirmation, contact support for verified deletion assistance.</p><p>Email <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a>, describing your request and account. We may need proportionate identity verification. Do not send identity documents unless securely requested. We will respond within the legally required period and explain any permitted refusal or extension.</p><p>You may complain directly to a relevant regulator without completing our support process first. In Zimbabwe, see <a href="https://www.potraz.gov.zw/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">POTRAZ, the Data Protection Authority (opens in a new tab)</a>.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>9. Children and third parties</h2><p>Account services are intended for adults aged 18 or over. If a child's information has been submitted, contact us so we can investigate and take appropriate action. Include referees' or other people's information only with a lawful basis and only where necessary.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>10. Updates and contact</h2><p>We will date revisions and give additional notice of material changes where required or appropriate. A new policy does not retrospectively authorise unrelated use of previously collected data. External services have their own notices.</p><p>Questions about storage, processing, correction, deletion or security? Contact <strong>Code Dev Solutions, Zimbabwe</strong> at <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a>. See our <a href="{{ route('terms') }}">Terms and Conditions</a> and <a href="{{ route('refund') }}">Refund Policy</a>.</p></section>
</article>
</x-public-layout>
